fact WorkItem(id: "WI-675", description: some(value: "scaland discrim tree has no DiscrimKey.RigidVar — a Rigid skolem over-matches and distinct skolems conflate. Rustland's DiscrimKey has a RigidVar(VarId) CONSTANT edge: a Rigid var keys as itself and matches only the same skolem, while flex Global / bound DeBruijn key as a wildcard var-edge. Scaland's DiscrimKey (scaland/core/src/main/scala/anthill/discrim/SubstTree.scala) has NO RigidVar case; Var.varId (term/Term.scala) collapses Global/DeBruijn/Rigid to one VarId and insertPatternWalk/queryNode add EVERY var kind as a wildcard var-edge on v.varId. Consequences once a Rigid reaches the tree: (a) a rigid GOAL var over-matches a concrete fact (should match only the same rigid); (b) two distinct skolems sharing the wildcard keyspace conflate. This also means the new viewsStructurallyEqual (WI-674) and the discrim tree DISAGREE about rigids — the comparator compares vars by full Var identity (rigid = constant), the tree treats rigid = wildcard; only the comparator is currently sound. UNREACHABLE TODAY: nothing in scaland mints a Var.Rigid (WI-637 added the kind as parity scaffolding only — no typer/proof-discharge). This WI must land BEFORE anything mints a Rigid. Scope: add DiscrimKey.RigidVar(vid: VarId); in the insert/query walkers, branch on Var kind (Rigid -> concrete RigidVar edge keyed by vid; Global/DeBruijn -> wildcard var-edge as today); mirror rustland kb/discrim.rs insert_walk/query_node RigidVar handling. Acceptance: sbt test green; new SubstTree tests pinning (1) a Rigid pattern var matches only the same-VarId Rigid, not a concrete fact and not a different-VarId Rigid; (2) a Global/DeBruijn var still matches anything; (3) discrim result agrees with viewsStructurallyEqual on a rigid-containing pair. Reference rustland kb/discrim.rs (DiscrimKey::RigidVar) and WI-637 (the Var kinds). Found during WI-674 step-1 code review."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

